  "body": "### Summary\nAs the author of the filtered lists and the personal smileys, I want the states #601 and #603 left out, so that the parsers do not guess them.\n\n### Scope\n1. The personal smiley page (`/user/uploadsmil.php`) of an account with all 11 slots filled, if one is available. The kit's accounts have 6 and 0, and no smiley is uploaded for this capture: uploading is a write that needs the operator's go.\n2. An `owntopic=1` or `owntopic=3` list that holds a sticky row. `R603a`-`R603d` have none; the sticky rows published are on `owntopic=2` (`R08-2`, `R603e`).\n3. Legacy oracles of `R603a`-`R603e`, run with `tooling/legacy-oracle/run-oracle.sh` at `2440d79`.\n\nPaging of a filtered list on other pages and forums is in #278, which this issue does not repeat.\n\n### Sources\n`docs/HFR-PROTOCOL.md` §6c \"Smiley page and filtered lists\", `MANIFEST.md` rows `R601a`-`R603f`.\n\n### Wanted by\n#427, #593, #592.\n\n### Acceptance criteria\nAnonymized fixtures and oracles committed, manifest and protocol entry updated, the *pending capture* marks removed.\n",
